{"id": "EUVD-2026-75246", "enisaUuid": "3cf1c4a1-9d7b-3b1a-a4e8-fc77542e3938", "description": "An unauthenticated remote attacker can craft a CORE protocol SESSION_REATTACH packet to steal an existing session and assume ongoing execution of the previously authenticated session.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Artemis: from 2.50.0 through 2.56.0; Apache ActiveMQ Artemis: from 1.0.0 through 2.44.0.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.57.0, which fixes the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-10T04:43:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T15:36:10", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/fxfjqrdsnksw5f17zs3yqo864lblgv6y"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-57967", "GHSA-735c-72gw-5q97"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 1.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17f46a60-b9ff-3031-9e17-ac5887872fcb", "product": {"name": "Apache ActiveMQ Artemis", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "1.0.0 \u22642.44.0"}, {"id": "5cacbea5-51b8-38f3-8a12-3257bfc4743b", "product": {"name": "Apache Artemis", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "2.50.0 \u22642.56.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a6155ff7-37b7-3edd-8f5f-62c758f258db", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}